        <description><![CDATA[{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Vinyl Cue Sheet\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Generates a vinyl cue-sheet from project regions/markers arranged in ruler lanes: one lane of regions defines the sides (e.g. !A, !B), another defines the track titles. Header details come from global settings; artist, album and audio format are read from the project. The cue sheet is written as HTML and converted to PDF when a converter (wkhtmltopdf or headless Chrome) is available on the system.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Actions:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Vinyl Cue Sheet \u8212- generate the cue sheet for the current project.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Vinyl Cue Sheet: Settings \u8212- edit the persistent global settings.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The settings editor uses ReaImGui when installed, otherwise a native dialog.\par}
}
]]></description>
